  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**The problem is nearly identical to Mex Tree (Min Version) except here you must find the maximum possible score**.\n\nYou have a tree with NNN vertices. A tree is a connected undirected acyclic graph on NNN vertices with N−1N - 1N−1 edges.\n\nYou want to assign **distinct labels** to the vertices of the tree. You will choose a permutation PPP of the integers [0,N−1][0, N - 1][0,N−1] and then assign the vertex XXX a label of PXP_XPX​.\n\nDefine MEX(S)MEX(S)MEX(S) for a set SSS, as the minimum non-negative integer not present in SSS. For example, MEX({1,0,2,2,4})=3MEX(\\{1, 0, 2, 2, 4\\}) = 3MEX({1,0,2,2,4})=3 and MEX({1})=0MEX(\\{1\\}) = 0MEX({1})=0.\n\nDefine f(u,v)f(u, v)f(u,v) as MEX({PX1,PX2,PX3,…,PXK})MEX(\\{P_{X_1}, P_{X_2}, P_{X_3}, \\ldots, P_{X_K}\\})MEX({PX1​​,PX2​​,PX3​​,…,PXK​​}) where X1,X2,…,XKX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_KX1​,X2​,…,XK​ are the vertices on the unique simple path from uuu to vvv (including uuu and vvv themselves, so X1=uX_1 = uX1​=u, XK=vX_K = vXK​=v).\n\nDefine scorescorescore of the tree as ∑X=1N∑Y=XNf(X,Y)\\sum_{X = 1}^{N} \\sum_{Y = X}^{N} f(X, Y)∑X=1N​∑Y=XN​f(X,Y), i.e. the sum of fff over all pairs of vertices.\n\nYou must find the **maximum** possible value of scorescorescore if you can suitably choose the permutation PPP.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe next N−1N - 1N−1 lines contain 222 integers each, uuu and vvv - representing an edge in the tree.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the **maximum possible score**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\le T \\le 501≤T≤50",
      "3≤N≤20003 \\le N \\le 20003≤N≤2000",
      "1≤u,v≤N1 \\le u, v \\le N1≤u,v≤N",
      "The set of input edges define a tree",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 200020002000."
    ],
