      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4",
        "output": "13\n11",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : We choose P=[3,0,1,2]P = [3, 0, 1, 2]P=[3,0,1,2]. The calculations are as follows:\n\nf(1,1)=0f(1, 1) = 0f(1,1)=0\nf(1,2)=1f(1, 2) = 1f(1,2)=1\nf(1,3)=2f(1, 3) = 2f(1,3)=2\nf(1,4)=4f(1, 4) = 4f(1,4)=4\nf(2,2)=1f(2, 2) = 1f(2,2)=1\nf(2,3)=2f(2, 3) = 2f(2,3)=2\nf(2,4)=3f(2, 4) = 3f(2,4)=3\nf(3,3)=0f(3, 3) = 0f(3,3)=0\nf(3,4)=0f(3, 4) = 0f(3,4)=0\nf(4,4)=0f(4, 4) = 0f(4,4)=0\n\nAdding the values, we get 1+2+4+1+2+3=131 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 3 = 131+2+4+1+2+3=13. It can be proven a larger score is impossible."
      }
